 wounded for 0.8 percent of Ukraine in 2025 | Russia-Ukraine war News | Al Jazeera","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/1/2/over-400000-russians-killed-wounded-for-0-8-percent-of-ukraine-in-2025"},{"title":"Russia denies think-tank assessment that 1.2 million of its troops have been killed or injured in Ukraine war | CBC News","url":"https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/russia-ukraine-war-dead-estimates-9.7064462"}]},"Based on the search results, here are the verified estimates for Russian casualties in the Ukraine war:\n\n## Key Verified Estimate\n\nRussia suffered 1.2 million casualties, including up to 325,000 troop deaths, between the start of Moscow's full-scale invasion in February 2022 and December 2025, according to a report from the Center for Strategic and International Studies (CSIS).\n\n## How These Estimates Were Compiled\n\nThe figures from the CSIS were compiled using the Washington, D.C.-based think tank's own analysis, data published by independent Russian news site Mediazona with the BBC, estimates by the British government and interviews with state officials. Mediazona, together with the BBC and a team of volunteers, has so far collected the names of over 160,000 troops killed by scouring news reports, social media and government websites.\n\n## Significance\n\nRussian forces have suffered approximately 1.2 million casualties (killed, wounded, and missing) and as many as 325,000 killed since February 2022. No major power has suffered anywhere near these numbers of casualties or fatalities in any war since World War II.\n\n## Additional Context\n\nThe report estimated that at current rates, combined Russian and Ukrainian casualties may be as high as 1.8 million and could reach 2 million by the spring."],"durationSeconds":6.257216500000002}}
[2026-02-04T18:06:42.982Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011fqJkZxqwatjmZQ9MVgyrz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"UK Ministry of Defence Russia casualties Ukraine assessment methodology\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"UK says Russian advances mask heavy losses and weak gains\",\"url\":\"https://ukdefencejournal.org.uk/uk-says-russian-advances-mask-heavy-losses-and-weak-gains/\"},{\"title\":\"British intelligence estimates overall Russian casualties in the Ukraine war at 1,118,000\",\"url\":\"https://www.ukrinform.net/rubric-ato/4047258-british-intelligence-estimates-overall-russian-casualties-in-the-ukraine-war-at-1118000.html\"},{\"title\":\"A Million Casualties for 1% of Territory: UK Slams Russia’s War Narrative\",\"url\":\"https://united24media.com/latest-news/a-million-casualties-for-1-of-territory-uk-slams-russias-war-narrative-14461\"},{\"title\":\"Russian casualties exceed 1.1m since invasion says Britain\",\"url\":\"https://ukdefencejournal.org.uk/russian-casualties-exceed-1-1m-since-invasion-says-britain/\"},{\"title\":\"The Russia-Ukraine War Report Card, Dec. 23, 2025 | Russia Matters\",\"url\":\"https://www.russiamatters.org/news/russia-ukraine-war-report-card/russia-ukraine-war-report-card-dec-23-2025\"},{\"title\":\"UK estimates half million Russian casualties in Ukraine\",\"url\":\"https://ukdefencejournal.org.uk/uk-estimates-half-million-russian-casualties-in-ukraine/\"},{\"title\":\"UK intelligence releases new estimate of Russia's losses in war | Ukrainska Pravda\",\"url\":\"https://www.pravda.com.ua/eng/news/2023/12/4/7431559/\"},{\"title\":\"Russian casualties have now likely hit the 1 million mark\",\"url\":\"https://ukdefencejournal.org.uk/russian-casualties-in-ukraine-have-now-likely-hit-the-1-million-mark/\"},{\"title\":\"Putin’s Ukraine War Is Killing Russia’s Poorest - The National Interest\",\"url\":\"https://nationalinterest.org/blog/buzz/putins-ukraine-war-is-killing-russias-poor-not-its-cities-sa-122525\"},{\"title\":\"Britain estimates 450,000 Russian troops killed or wounded\",\"url\":\"https://ukdefencejournal.org.uk/britain-estimates-450000-russian-troops-killed-or-wounded/\"}]\n\nI found information about UK Ministry of Defence assessments of Russian casualties in Ukraine. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Casualty Assessments\n\nBritain's Ministry of Defence has assessed that Russia has likely sustained approximately 1,140,000 casualties, both killed and wounded, since launching its full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022. The update draws on Ukrainian General Staff reporting and recorded an average of 1,008 Russian casualties per day during October.\n\n## Assessment Methodology\n\nWhile the search results don't explicitly detail the UK Ministry of Defence's specific methodology, they do provide some insight into how assessments are conducted:\n\n1. **Data Source**: The UK updates draw on Ukrainian General Staff reporting, suggesting collaboration between intelligence agencies.\n\n2. **Operational Analysis**: The elevated casualty rate is highly likely a reflection of Russia's ongoing attritional offensive across a wide front, with most Russian forces receiving only limited training and being unable to carry out complex offensive operations, resulting in small-scale but costly wave attacks.\n\n3. **Intelligence Caveats**: UK Defence Intelligence stated that even among Russian officials, there is probably a low level of understanding of the total casualties number due to a long-standing culture of dishonest reporting in the army.\n\nThe UK appears to track both killed and wounded figures, analyze tactical patterns to understand casualty rates, and acknowledge the challenges in verifying exact numbers given Russian reporting practices.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffdb2836-5730-4184-8318-1c286009c5ec","uuid":"ec0d3c39-c9f4-489e-aae9-c9ed249eb117","tool_use_result":{"query":"UK Ministry of Defence Russia casualties Ukraine assessment methodology","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_017wt4dXio1dvh3Lm2p9ZKsT","content":[{"title":"UK says Russian advances mask heavy losses and weak gains","url":"https://ukdefencejournal.org.uk/uk-says-russian-advances-mask-heavy-losses-and-weak-gains/"},{"title":"British intelligence estimates overall Russian casualties in the Ukraine war at 1,118,000","url":"https://www.ukrinform.net/rubric-ato/4047258-british-intelligence-estimates-overall-russian-casualties-in-the-ukraine-war-at-1118000.html"},{"title":"A Million Casualties for 1% of Territory: UK Slams Russia’s War Narrative","url":"https://united24media.com/latest-news/a-million-casualties-for-1-of-territory-uk-slams-russias-war-narrative-14461"},{"title":"Russian casualties exceed 1.1m since invasion says Britain","url":"https://ukdefencejournal.org.uk/russian-casualties-exceed-1-1m-since-invasion-says-britain/"},{"title":"The Russia-Ukraine War Report Card, Dec. 23, 2025 | Russia Matters","url":"https://www.russiamatters.org/news/russia-ukraine-war-report-card/russia-ukraine-war-report-card-dec-23-2025"},{"title":"UK estimates half million Russian casualties in Ukraine","url":"https://ukdefencejournal.org.uk/uk-estimates-half-million-russian-casualties-in-ukraine/"},{"title":"UK intelligence releases new estimate of Russia's losses in war | Ukrainska Pravda","url":"https://www.pravda.com.ua/eng/news/2023/12/4/7431559/"},{"title":"Russian casualties have now likely hit the 1 million mark","url":"https://ukdefencejournal.org.uk/russian-casualties-in-ukraine-have-now-likely-hit-the-1-million-mark/"},{"title":"Putin’s Ukraine War Is Killing Russia’s Poorest - The National Interest","url":"https://nationalinterest.org/blog/buzz/putins-ukraine-war-is-killing-russias-poor-not-its-cities-sa-122525"},{"title":"Britain estimates 450,000 Russian troops killed or wounded","url":"https://ukdefencejournal.org.uk/britain-estimates-450000-russian-troops-killed-or-wounded/"}]},"I found information about UK Ministry of Defence assessments of Russian casualties in Ukraine. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Casualty Assessments\n\nBritain's Ministry of Defence has assessed that Russia has likely sustained approximately 1,140,000 casualties, both killed and wounded, since launching its full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022. The update draws on Ukrainian General Staff reporting and recorded an average of 1,008 Russian casualties per day during October.\n\n## Assessment Methodology\n\nWhile the search results don't explicitly detail the UK Ministry of Defence's specific methodology, they do provide some insight into how assessments are conducted:\n\n1. **Data Source**: The UK updates draw on Ukrainian General Staff reporting, suggesting collaboration between intelligence agencies.\n\n2. **Operational Analysis**: The elevated casualty rate is highly likely a reflection of Russia's ongoing attritional offensive across a wide front, with most Russian forces receiving only limited training and being unable to carry out complex offensive operations, resulting in small-scale but costly wave attacks.\n\n3. **Intelligence Caveats**: UK Defence Intelligence stated that even among Russian officials, there is probably a low level of understanding of the total casualties number due to a long-standing culture of dishonest reporting in the army.\n\nThe UK appears to track both killed and wounded figures, analyze tactical patterns to understand casualty rates, and acknowledge the challenges in verifying exact numbers given Russian reporting practices."],"durationSeconds":7.029442800000001}}
[2026-02-04T18:06:44.221Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AAm7uCvx4Us8ebw6gcW4Eo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Ukraine General Staff daily Russian losses killed wounded methodology\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Casualties of the Russo-Ukrainian war - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casualties_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war\"},{\"title\":\"Russian losses in the war with Ukraine. Mediazona count, updated\",\"url\":\"https://en.zona.media/article/2026/01/16/casualties_eng-trl\"},{\"title\":\"What is the monthly casualty rate for the Russian army...\",\"url\":\"https://factually.co/fact-checks/military/monthly-casualty-rate-russian-army-war-in-ukraine-c1f921\"},{\"title\":\"Frontline report: Russia has lost over 1% of all men in the country to its war in Ukraine - Euromaidan Press\",\"url\":\"https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/12/21/frontline-report-2025-12-21/\"},{\"title\":\"Casualties of Russia in Ukraine - official data\",\"url\":\"https://index.minfin.com.ua/en/russian-invading/casualties/\"},{\"title\":\"Ukrainian General Staff Reports Russian Losses Near 1.2 Million in 2025 War | Ukraine news - #Mezha\",\"url\":\"https://mezha.net/eng/bukvy/ukrainian-general-staff-reports-russian-losses-near-1-2-million-in-2025-war/\"},{\"title\":\"Russia’s Battlefield Woes in Ukraine | CSIS\",\"url\":\"https://www.csis.org/analysis/russias-battlefield-woes-ukraine\"},{\"title\":\"Russia Has Lost 1.2 Million Troops in Ukraine—More Than Its Entire Pre-War Army\",\"url\":\"https://united24media.com/war-in-ukraine/russia-has-lost-12-million-troops-in-ukraine-more-than-its-entire-pre-war-army-14361\"},{\"title\":\"Russian losses over past day: 780 soldiers killed and wounded | Ukrainska Pravda\",\"url\":\"https://www.pravda.com.ua/eng/news/2026/02/04/8019337/\"},{\"title\":\"The Russia-Ukraine War Report Card, Dec. 23, 2025 | Russia Matters\",\"url\":\"https://www.russiamatters.org/news/russia-ukraine-war-report-card/russia-ukraine-war-report-card-dec-23-2025\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Ukraine's General Staff daily reports on Russian losses and their methodology:\n\n## Daily Reporting Process\n\nThe General Staff of the Armed Forces of Ukraine regularly reports Russian losses killed and wounded over the past day, along with weapons and military equipment losses. Day after day, casualty updates add between 1,000 and 1,700 men, reflecting ongoing daily tracking.\n\n## Methodology and Data Sources\n\nDiscrepancies in casualty reports stem from differing definitions (casualties = killed + wounded vs killed only), time windows (daily spikes vs smoothed monthly averages), and source types (official Russian secrecy, Ukrainian General Staff tallies, open-source verifications, and intelligence leaks). Kyiv emphasizes that official figures from Russia are not published, and intelligence analysts base their assessments on various sources.\n\n## Classification of Losses\n\nThe totals include both those killed and severely wounded who will never return to combat—hence the classification as \"irrecoverable losses\". Early in the war, more troops were wounded than killed, but that trend has now reversed.\n\n## Current Scale\n\nAverage daily losses of Russia during November 2025 reached 1,033, according to the General Staff of Ukraine, and Ukrainian General Staff reports Russian military losses in the full-scale war reaching approximately 1.2 million casualties, including killed and wounded, as of December 23, 2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffdb2836-5730-4184-8318-1c286009c5ec","uuid":"385cf151-2fb5-4a99-8bf1-4f772da90fc2","tool_use_result":{"query":"Ukraine General Staff daily Russian losses killed wounded methodology","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019sacwiuJA8cgPhJmQdYuvJ","content":[{"title":"Casualties of the Russo-Ukrainian war - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casualties_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war"},{"title":"Russian losses in the war with Ukraine. Mediazona count, updated","url":"https://en.zona.media/article/2026/01/16/casualties_eng-trl"},{"title":"What is the monthly casualty rate for the Russian army...","url":"https://factually.co/fact-checks/military/monthly-casualty-rate-russian-army-war-in-ukraine-c1f921"},{"title":"Frontline report: Russia has lost over 1% of all men in the country to its war in Ukraine - Euromaidan Press","url":"https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/12/21/frontline-report-2025-12-21/"},{"title":"Casualties of Russia in Ukraine - official data","url":"https://index.minfin.com.ua/en/russian-invading/casualties/"},{"title":"Ukrainian General Staff Reports Russian Losses Near 1.2 Million in 2025 War | Ukraine news - #Mezha","url":"https://mezha.net/eng/bukvy/ukrainian-general-staff-reports-russian-losses-near-1-2-million-in-2025-war/"},{"title":"Russia’s Battlefield Woes in Ukraine | CSIS","url":"https://www.csis.org/analysis/russias-battlefield-woes-ukraine"},{"title":"Russia Has Lost 1.2 Million Troops in Ukraine—More Than Its Entire Pre-War Army","url":"https://united24media.com/war-in-ukraine/russia-has-lost-12-million-troops-in-ukraine-more-than-its-entire-pre-war-army-14361"},{"title":"Russian losses over past day: 780 soldiers killed and wounded | Ukrainska Pravda","url":"https://www.pravda.com.ua/eng/news/2026/02/04/8019337/"},{"title":"The Russia-Ukraine War Report Card, Dec. 23, 2025 | Russia Matters","url":"https://www.russiamatters.org/news/russia-ukraine-war-report-card/russia-ukraine-war-report-card-dec-23-2025"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about Ukraine's General Staff daily reports on Russian losses and their methodology:\n\n## Daily Reporting Process\n\nThe General Staff of the Armed Forces of Ukraine regularly reports Russian losses killed and wounded over the past day, along with weapons and military equipment losses. Day after day, casualty updates add between 1,000 and 1,700 men, reflecting ongoing daily tracking.\n\n## Methodology and Data Sources\n\nDiscrepancies in casualty reports stem from differing definitions (casualties = killed + wounded vs killed only), time windows (daily spikes vs smoothed monthly averages), and source types (official Russian secrecy, Ukrainian General Staff tallies, open-source verifications, and intelligence leaks). Kyiv emphasizes that official figures from Russia are not published, and intelligence analysts base their assessments on various sources.\n\n## Classification of Losses\n\nThe totals include both those killed and severely wounded who will never return to combat—hence the classification as \"irrecoverable losses\". Early in the war, more troops were wounded than killed, but that trend has now reversed.\n\n## Current Scale\n\nAverage daily losses of Russia during November 2025 reached 1,033, according to the General Staff of Ukraine, and Ukrainian General Staff reports Russian military losses in the full-scale war reaching approximately 1.2 million casualties, including killed and wounded, as of December 23, 2025."],"durationSeconds":7.682091399999999}}
[2026-02-04T18:06:45.028Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013JE8Snds5D73H8xMmywXAJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"US intelligence Russia Ukraine casualty estimates Pentagon assessment\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Pentagon Estimates Thousands of Russian Troops Have Been Killed in Ukraine | Military.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.military.com/daily-news/2022/03/08/pentagon-estimates-thousands-of-russian-troops-have-been-killed-ukraine.html\"},{\"title\":\"U.S. quietly sharing its estimate of Russian war casualties: More than 75,000 killed or injured | The Seattle Times\",\"url\":\"https://www.seattletimes.com/nation-world/u-s-quietly-sharing-its-estimate-of-russian-war-casualties-more-than-75000-killed-or-injured/\"},{\"title\":\"Declassified US Intelligence Reveals Massive Russian Losses in Ukraine\",\"url\":\"https://www.voanews.com/a/declassified-us-intelligence-reveals-massive-russian-losses-in-ukraine/7395271.html\"},{\"title\":\"Casualties of the Russo-Ukrainian war - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casualties_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war\"},{\"title\":\"Pentagon estimates 2,000 to 4,000 Russian soldiers killed in Ukraine\",\"url\":\"https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20220308-pentagon-estimates-2-000-to-4-000-russian-soldiers-killed-in-ukraine\"},{\"title\":\"Pentagon's leaked intelligence documents: US estimates Russian and Ukrainian losses in war at 354,000\",\"url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/pentagons-leaked-intelligence-documents-us-194035171.html\"},{\"title\":\"“Ukraine War Causalities Near Half a Million, U.S. Officials Say”\",\"url\":\"https://www.congress.gov/118/meeting/house/116768/documents/HHRG-118-ZS00-20240130-SD002.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"U.S. Intel Says 315K Russian Casualties in Ukraine – Congress Source - The Moscow Times\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2023/12/12/us-intel-says-315k-russian-casualties-in-ukraine-congress-source-a83402\"},{\"title\":\"The Russia-Ukraine War Report Card, Jan. 14, 2026 | Russia Matters\",\"url\":\"https://www.russiamatters.org/news/russia-ukraine-war-report-card/russia-ukraine-war-report-card-jan-14-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Estimating conflict losses and reporting biases | PNAS\",\"url\":\"https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2307372120\"}]\n\nI've found comprehensive information about US intelligence and Pentagon assessments of casualty estimates in the Russia-Ukraine war. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Early Assessments (March 2022)\n\nThe Defense Intelligence Agency assessed that between 2,000 and 4,000 Russian troops had been killed in the first two weeks of the invasion, based on a mix of intelligence sources and open source information.\n\n## Mid-War Estimates (2022-2023)\n\nThe CIA director estimated that 60,000 Russian soldiers had been killed or injured. By mid-2023, Pentagon leaked documents showed Russia's losses were estimated at 35,500-43,000 killed in battle and 154,180 wounded, with a total of 189,500-223,000.\n\n## Late 2023 Assessments\n\nIn July 2022, CIA director Bill Burns said U.S. intelligence estimated that Russian losses were \"in the vicinity of 15,000 killed and maybe three times that wounded.\" By December 2023, assessments had grown significantly.\n\n## Recent 2024-2025 Estimates\n\nAccording to U.S. officials in early 2024, Russia's military casualties were approaching 300,000, including as many as 120,000 deaths and 170,000 to 180,000 injured troops.\n\nMore than 750,000 killed or injured were estimated according to a March 2025 estimate by the U.S. intelligence community. According to ex-CIA director William Burns' January 2026 interview, Russia had suffered 1,100,000 casualties.\n\n## Important Caveats\n\nOfficials cautioned that casualty figures remained difficult to estimate because Moscow is believed to routinely undercount its war dead and injured, and Kyiv does not disclose official figures.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffdb2836-5730-4184-8318-1c286009c5ec","uuid":"8346433a-3922-4485-ae94-92e7a16af387","tool_use_result":{"query":"US intelligence Russia Ukraine casualty estimates Pentagon assessment","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_017cZLWWhH6x75KrvfZsBqUD","content":[{"title":"Pentagon Estimates Thousands of Russian Troops Have Been Killed in Ukraine | Military.com","url":"https://www.military.com/daily-news/2022/03/08/pentagon-estimates-thousands-of-russian-troops-have-been-killed-ukraine.html"},{"title":"U.S. quietly sharing its estimate of Russian war casualties: More than 75,000 killed or injured | The Seattle Times","url":"https://www.seattletimes.com/nation-world/u-s-quietly-sharing-its-estimate-of-russian-war-casualties-more-than-75000-killed-or-injured/"},{"title":"Declassified US Intelligence Reveals Massive Russian Losses in Ukraine","url":"https://www.voanews.com/a/declassified-us-intelligence-reveals-massive-russian-losses-in-ukraine/7395271.html"},{"title":"Casualties of the Russo-Ukrainian war - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casualties_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war"},{"title":"Pentagon estimates 2,000 to 4,000 Russian soldiers killed in Ukraine","url":"https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20220308-pentagon-estimates-2-000-to-4-000-russian-soldiers-killed-in-ukraine"},{"title":"Pentagon's leaked intelligence documents: US estimates Russian and Ukrainian losses in war at 354,000","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/pentagons-leaked-intelligence-documents-us-194035171.html"},{"title":"“Ukraine War Causalities Near Half a Million, U.S. Officials Say”","url":"https://www.congress.gov/118/meeting/house/116768/documents/HHRG-118-ZS00-20240130-SD002.pdf"},{"title":"U.S. Intel Says 315K Russian Casualties in Ukraine – Congress Source - The Moscow Times","url":"https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2023/12/12/us-intel-says-315k-russian-casualties-in-ukraine-congress-source-a83402"},{"title":"The Russia-Ukraine War Report Card, Jan. 14, 2026 | Russia Matters","url":"https://www.russiamatters.org/news/russia-ukraine-war-report-card/russia-ukraine-war-report-card-jan-14-2026"},{"title":"Estimating conflict losses and reporting biases | PNAS","url":"https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2307372120"}]},"I've found comprehensive information about US intelligence and Pentagon assessments of casualty estimates in the Russia-Ukraine war. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Early Assessments (March 2022)\n\nThe Defense Intelligence Agency assessed that between 2,000 and 4,000 Russian troops had been killed in the first two weeks of the invasion, based on a mix of intelligence sources and open source information.\n\n## Mid-War Estimates (2022-2023)\n\nThe CIA director estimated that 60,000 Russian soldiers had been killed or injured. By mid-2023, Pentagon leaked documents showed Russia's losses were estimated at 35,500-43,000 killed in battle and 154,180 wounded, with a total of 189,500-223,000.\n\n## Late 2023 Assessments\n\nIn July 2022, CIA director Bill Burns said U.S. intelligence estimated that Russian losses were \"in the vicinity of 15,000 killed and maybe three times that wounded.\" By December 2023, assessments had grown significantly.\n\n## Recent 2024-2025 Estimates\n\nAccording to U.S. officials in early 2024, Russia's military casualties were approaching 300,000, including as many as 120,000 deaths and 170,000 to 180,000 injured troops.\n\nMore than 750,000 killed or injured were estimated according to a March 2025 estimate by the U.S. intelligence community. According to ex-CIA director William Burns' January 2026 interview, Russia had suffered 1,100,000 casualties.\n\n## Important Caveats\n\nOfficials cautioned that casualty figures remained difficult to estimate because Moscow is believed to routinely undercount its war dead and injured, and Kyiv does not disclose official figures."],"durationSeconds":7.745769299999998}}
[2026-02-04T18:06:46.170Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DRXT4ESr9tkgKMx9qU8S63","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Russian official casualty figures Ukraine war Shoigu Putin statements\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Russia’s Battlefield Woes in Ukraine | CSIS\",\"url\":\"https://www.csis.org/analysis/russias-battlefield-woes-ukraine\"},{\"title\":\"Casualties of the Russo-Ukrainian war - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casualties_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war\"},{\"title\":\"Russia faces a heavy price for limited gains in Ukraine war, death toll estimates suggest\",\"url\":\"https://www.nbcnews.com/world/ukraine/russia-faces-heavy-price-limited-gains-ukraine-war-death-toll-estimate-rcna256260\"},{\"title\":\"Russia-Ukraine War - Costs and casualties: the price of Putin’s war | Britannica\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/event/2022-Russian-invasion-of-Ukraine/Costs-and-casualties-the-price-of-Putins-war\"},{\"title\":\"Over 400,000 Russians killed, wounded for 0.8 percent of Ukraine in 2025 | Russia-Ukraine war News | Al Jazeera\",\"url\":\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/1/2/over-400000-russians-killed-wounded-for-0-8-percent-of-ukraine-in-2025\"},{\"title\":\"As Russia’s Military Losses Pass 1 Million, Putin Says All Were “For a Cause”\",\"url\":\"https://united24media.com/latest-news/as-russias-military-losses-pass-1-million-putin-says-all-were-for-a-cause-10375\"},{\"title\":\"Putin Admits Russia Has Suffered Huge Losses in Ukraine - Newsweek\",\"url\":\"https://www.newsweek.com/putin-admits-russia-suffered-huge-losses-ukraine-1852660\"},{\"title\":\"Putin makes rare claim on Ukraine war casualties\",\"url\":\"https://thehill.com/policy/defense/4708836-putin-russian-ukraine-war-casualties/\"},{\"title\":\"Russian losses in the war with Ukraine. Mediazona count, updated\",\"url\":\"https://en.zona.media/article/2026/01/30/casualties_eng-trl\"},{\"title\":\"Putin Issues Rare Statement on Ukraine War Losses - Newsweek\",\"url\":\"https://www.newsweek.com/putin-rare-statement-ukraine-war-losses-casualties-1908869\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding Russian official casualty figures and statements from Putin and Shoigu:\n\n## Official Russian Statements\n\nIn September 2022, in the Russian government's only official statement on losses suffered during the \"special military operation,\" Defense Minister Sergei Shoigu claimed that 5,937 Russian troops had been killed in action. More recently, the latest official statements from the Russian side came years ago when then-Defense Minister Sergei Shoigu estimated in the fall of 2022 that Russia had lost nearly 6,000 troops.\n\n## Putin's Statements on Casualties\n\nPutin has been reluctant to acknowledge significant losses. In October, Putin said that while Russia sustains losses, they are \"many times\" smaller than those suffered by Ukraine. More recently, at a meeting in St. Petersburg, Putin told the heads of several international news agencies that there are 1,348 Russian troops and officers in captivity in Ukraine compared to the 6,465 Ukrainians in Russian detention, and asserted that Moscow has only lost one soldier for every five that Kyiv has.\n\n## Discrepancy with Western Estimates\n\nBoth Russia and Ukraine generally do not report their casualty numbers, but both sides tend to underestimate their deaths while saying the other side's losses far exceed their own. Western estimates paint a very different picture. Overall, a high of 250,000 Russian soldiers have died in Ukraine, with over 950,000 total Russian casualties.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffdb2836-5730-4184-8318-1c286009c5ec","uuid":"a29195e2-a8f3-43d2-97a8-ce3ff66dc762","tool_use_result":{"query":"Russian official casualty figures Ukraine war Shoigu Putin statements","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01UpZY6WtnrCRuQhar3SBeME","content":[{"title":"Russia’s Battlefield Woes in Ukraine | CSIS","url":"https://www.csis.org/analysis/russias-battlefield-woes-ukraine"},{"title":"Casualties of the Russo-Ukrainian war - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casualties_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war"},{"title":"Russia faces a heavy price for limited gains in Ukraine war, death toll estimates suggest","url":"https://www.nbcnews.com/world/ukraine/russia-faces-heavy-price-limited-gains-ukraine-war-death-toll-estimate-rcna256260"},{"title":"Russia-Ukraine War - Costs and casualties: the price of Putin’s war | Britannica","url":"https://www.britannica.com/event/2022-Russian-invasion-of-Ukraine/Costs-and-casualties-the-price-of-Putins-war"},{"title":"Over 400,000 Russians killed, wounded for 0.8 percent of Ukraine in 2025 | Russia-Ukraine war News | Al Jazeera","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/1/2/over-400000-russians-killed-wounded-for-0-8-percent-of-ukraine-in-2025"},{"title":"As Russia’s Military Losses Pass 1 Million, Putin Says All Were “For a Cause”","url":"https://united24media.com/latest-news/as-russias-military-losses-pass-1-million-putin-says-all-were-for-a-cause-10375"},{"title":"Putin Admits Russia Has Suffered Huge Losses in Ukraine - Newsweek","url":"https://www.newsweek.com/putin-admits-russia-suffered-huge-losses-ukraine-1852660"},{"title":"Putin makes rare claim on Ukraine war casualties","url":"https://thehill.com/policy/defense/4708836-putin-russian-ukraine-war-casualties/"},{"title":"Russian losses in the war with Ukraine. Mediazona count, updated","url":"https://en.zona.media/article/2026/01/30/casualties_eng-trl"},{"title":"Putin Issues Rare Statement on Ukraine War Losses - Newsweek","url":"https://www.newsweek.com/putin-rare-statement-ukraine-war-losses-casualties-1908869"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found regarding Russian official casualty figures and statements from Putin and Shoigu:\n\n## Official Russian Statements\n\nIn September 2022, in the Russian government's only official statement on losses suffered during the \"special military operation,\" Defense Minister Sergei Shoigu claimed that 5,937 Russian troops had been killed in action. More recently, the latest official statements from the Russian side came years ago when then-Defense Minister Sergei Shoigu estimated in the fall of 2022 that Russia had lost nearly 6,000 troops.\n\n## Putin's Statements on Casualties\n\nPutin has been reluctant to acknowledge significant losses. In October, Putin said that while Russia sustains losses, they are \"many times\" smaller than those suffered by Ukraine. More recently, at a meeting in St. Petersburg, Putin told the heads of several international news agencies that there are 1,348 Russian troops and officers in captivity in Ukraine compared to the 6,465 Ukrainians in Russian detention, and asserted that Moscow has only lost one soldier for every five that Kyiv has.\n\n## Discrepancy with Western Estimates\n\nBoth Russia and Ukraine generally do not report their casualty numbers, but both sides tend to underestimate their deaths while saying the other side's losses far exceed their own. Western estimates paint a very different picture. Overall, a high of 250,000 Russian soldiers have died in Ukraine, with over 950,000 total Russian casualties."],"durationSeconds":7.7469624}}
[2026-02-04T18:06:46.488Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UTa7E2pT88g3bqQZxKtSLp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"independent open source intelligence Russia casualties Oryx Mediazona\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Open-source intelligence in the Russian invasion of Ukraine - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open-source_intelligence_in_the_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine\"},{\"title\":\"Oryx (website) - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oryx_(website)\"},{\"title\":\"Mediazona confrims deaths of 15 Russian officers. They all died in a fire in Zaporizhzhia region, four more are awaiting confirmation\",\"url\":\"https://en.zona.media/article/2025/12/10/officers\"},{\"title\":\"Russian losses in the war with Ukraine. Mediazona count, updated\",\"url\":\"https://en.zona.media/article/2026/01/16/casualties_eng-trl\"},{\"title\":\"Over 160,000 Russian soldiers estimated killed since start of full-scale invasion of Ukraine\",\"url\":\"https://theins.ru/en/news/279102\"},{\"title\":\"Russian equipment losses in Ukraine surpass 15,000, says Oryx OSINT group\",\"url\":\"https://kyivindependent.com/russian-equipment-losses-in-ukraine-surpass-15-000-says-oryx-osint-group/\"},{\"title\":\"Russian Tank Losses in Ukraine Hit 1,000 – Open Source Analysis - The Moscow Times\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2022/09/06/russian-tank-losses-in-ukraine-hit-1000-open-source-analysis-a78727\"},{\"title\":\"Open-source data shows Russia’s equipment losses in Ukraine reached a two-year high in October — Meduza\",\"url\":\"https://meduza.io/en/feature/2024/11/05/open-source-data-shows-russia-s-equipment-losses-in-ukraine-reached-a-two-year-high-in-october\"},{\"title\":\"Open-source intelligence in the Russian invasion of Ukraine | Military Wiki | Fandom\",\"url\":\"https://military-history.fandom.com/wiki/Open-source_intelligence_in_the_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine\"},{\"title\":\"Oryx\",\"url\":\"https://www.oryxspioenkop.com/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about independent open-source intelligence tracking of Russia casualties, particularly Oryx and Mediazona:\n\n## Oryx\n\nOryx is a Dutch open-source intelligence defence analysis website and warfare research group. Oryx gained international prominence through its work during the Russian invasion of Ukraine, counting and keeping track of material losses based on visual evidence and OSINT from social media. It has been regularly cited in major media, including Reuters, BBC News, The Guardian, The Economist, Newsweek, CNN, and CBS News. Because it reports only visually confirmed losses, Oryx's tallies of equipment losses have formed absolute minimum baselines for loss estimates.\n\n## Mediazona\n\nMediazona, working with the BBC's Russian service and a team of volunteers, has been compiling and maintaining a named list of the Russian military dead built from publicly available, verifiable sources, such as social media posts by relatives, reports in local media, and statements from regional authorities. Using open sources, Mediazona was able to confirm the mass death of officers from the headquarters of the 35th Combined Arms Army during a fire in the Zaporizhzhia region.\n\nMediazona has released information concerning 95,323 confirmed Russian military deaths identified through an ongoing open-source intelligence (OSINT) investigation conducted in partnership with BBC News Russian and a team of volunteers. Experts interviewed by the BBC stressed that the actual death toll is likely much higher than confirmed figures suggest, as only 45 to 65% of Russian fatalities in Ukraine are believed to have been documented.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffdb2836-5730-4184-8318-1c286009c5ec","uuid":"5a143911-2be3-4de5-9521-caf54b2be70f","tool_use_result":{"query":"independent open source intelligence Russia casualties Oryx Mediazona","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011M8RdvmjfPxDq1UXm4rZg8","content":[{"title":"Open-source intelligence in the Russian invasion of Ukraine - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open-source_intelligence_in_the_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine"},{"title":"Oryx (website) - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oryx_(website)"},{"title":"Mediazona confrims deaths of 15 Russian officers. They all died in a fire in Zaporizhzhia region, four more are awaiting confirmation","url":"https://en.zona.media/article/2025/12/10/officers"},{"title":"Russian losses in the war with Ukraine. Mediazona count, updated","url":"https://en.zona.media/article/2026/01/16/casualties_eng-trl"},{"title":"Over 160,000 Russian soldiers estimated killed since start of full-scale invasion of Ukraine","url":"https://theins.ru/en/news/279102"},{"title":"Russian equipment losses in Ukraine surpass 15,000, says Oryx OSINT group","url":"https://kyivindependent.com/russian-equipment-losses-in-ukraine-surpass-15-000-says-oryx-osint-group/"},{"title":"Russian Tank Losses in Ukraine Hit 1,000 – Open Source Analysis - The Moscow Times","url":"https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2022/09/06/russian-tank-losses-in-ukraine-hit-1000-open-source-analysis-a78727"},{"title":"Open-source data shows Russia’s equipment losses in Ukraine reached a two-year high in October — Meduza","url":"https://meduza.io/en/feature/2024/11/05/open-source-data-shows-russia-s-equipment-losses-in-ukraine-reached-a-two-year-high-in-october"},{"title":"Open-source intelligence in the Russian invasion of Ukraine | Military Wiki | Fandom","url":"https://military-history.fandom.com/wiki/Open-source_intelligence_in_the_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine"},{"title":"Oryx","url":"https://www.oryxspioenkop.com/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about independent open-source intelligence tracking of Russia casualties, particularly Oryx and Mediazona:\n\n## Oryx\n\nOryx is a Dutch open-source intelligence defence analysis website and warfare research group. Oryx gained international prominence through its work during the Russian invasion of Ukraine, counting and keeping track of material losses based on visual evidence and OSINT from social media. It has been regularly cited in major media, including Reuters, BBC News, The Guardian, The Economist, Newsweek, CNN, and CBS News. Because it reports only visually confirmed losses, Oryx's tallies of equipment losses have formed absolute minimum baselines for loss estimates.\n\n## Mediazona\n\nMediazona, working with the BBC's Russian service and a team of volunteers, has been compiling and maintaining a named list of the Russian military dead built from publicly available, verifiable sources, such as social media posts by relatives, reports in local media, and statements from regional authorities. Using open sources, Mediazona was able to confirm the mass death of officers from the headquarters of the 35th Combined Arms Army during a fire in the Zaporizhzhia region.\n\nMediazona has released information concerning 95,323 confirmed Russian military deaths identified through an ongoing open-source intelligence (OSINT) investigation conducted in partnership with BBC News Russian and a team of volunteers. Experts interviewed by the BBC stressed that the actual death toll is likely much higher than confirmed figures suggest, as only 45 to 65% of Russian fatalities in Ukraine are believed to have been documented."],"durationSeconds":8.5941214}}
